#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133505 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04b8c8285d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "0c2486d6-bb55-52ba-9fd8-6b516d3f7858" :question/math-academy-id "e-5557" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ be vectors such that $\\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert = 6$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{u}+4\\mathbf{v} \\Vert = 25.$  If $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v},$ find $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v},$ we also have that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $4\\mathbf{v}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+4v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+‖4v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+4v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+(4‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖u+4v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+16‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (25)^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+16(6)^{2} \\\\ 625 & =‖u{‖}^{2}+576 \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =625-576 \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{u}=\\Vert\\mathbf{u}\\Vert^2=49.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133506 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae3aec8-4d20-5467-9ced-2a9c1bda3afd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minimum Value Using the Triangle Inequality"}] :question/id #uuid "112253ae-e0ea-554a-83bf-87f8ba7c9ce7" :question/math-academy-id "e-5558" :question/problem "Given that $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} +3\\mathbf{v} \\Vert=14$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert=2,$ find the smallest possible value of $\\Vert \\mathbf{u}\\Vert.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+3v‖ & \\le ‖u‖+‖3v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+3v‖ & \\le ‖u‖+3‖v‖ \\\\ 14 & \\le ‖u‖+3(2) \\\\ 14 & \\le ‖u‖+6 \\\\ 8 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ is $8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133507 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2391612a-ee27-5cb2-a194-9b51e6fec1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Pythagorean Theorem and the Cauchy-Schwarz and Triangle Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "5e72235b-a419-5f27-bee7-01be8b49c997" :question/math-academy-id "e-5559" :question/problem "Let the vectors $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}|^2+5\\Vert\\mathbf{v}+\\mathbf{w}\\Vert^2=29$ and $\\| \\mathbf{u} \\|  = \\| \\mathbf{w} \\| = 2$, then what is the minimum possible value of $\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert?$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}29 & =|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =4‖v{‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{w}$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4‖v{‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =4‖v{‖}^{2}+5(‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2}) \\\\  & \\le 4‖v{‖}^{2}+5(‖v{‖}^{2}+{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}29 & \\le 9‖v{‖}^{2}+20 \\\\ 9 & \\le 9‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 1 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $1 \\leq \\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert^2$ implies that $1 \\leq \\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert$. Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert$ is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae3aec8-4d20-5467-9ced-2a9c1bda3afd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minimum Value Using the Triangle Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c67f5c8-ace8-5d01-a0dd-292ecf67870e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309706} {:answer/id #uuid "594a6210-b380-585c-bf83-0bf3c729789b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309707} {:answer/id #uuid "de2b02ea-174b-5122-9453-c66727e62db9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309708} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ef221d-834b-52cb-8252-7ccbb7b48aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309709} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc4b75e-26da-5fcb-b923-3c0df7170a19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3ef221d-834b-52cb-8252-7ccbb7b48aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309709} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7847158-31d8-5468-ac51-329fb39a9f45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65b81769-10fa-5dce-86a3-3a97e46cc0ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-140459" :question/problem "Given that $‖5u-4v‖=26$ and $‖u‖=2$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖5u-4v‖ & \\le ‖5u‖+‖-4v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖5u-4v‖ & \\le 5‖u‖+4‖v‖ \\\\ 26 & \\le 5\\cdot 2+4‖v‖ \\\\ 26 & \\le 10+4‖v‖ \\\\ 16 & \\le 4‖v‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$ is $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae3aec8-4d20-5467-9ced-2a9c1bda3afd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minimum Value Using the Triangle Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2071aabd-618e-569f-b73b-989dc48bdb26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309713} {:answer/id #uuid "72848d2c-54f4-5136-af9d-c502b2769999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309714} {:answer/id #uuid "1c662eab-1b88-5443-9ff9-2c6a776a6d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309715} {:answer/id #uuid "4711151d-c1d3-5cf2-b399-74aace034e93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309716} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ab5440-d9a2-5b95-ab4e-3c60f42b5523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72848d2c-54f4-5136-af9d-c502b2769999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309714} :answer-field/id #uuid "38bab780-815a-5ddd-ab2a-88f8bab428ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ebf76a0-eec1-5d1b-be4c-48f860555f1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140460" :question/problem "Given that $‖8u-v‖=35$ and $‖v‖=11$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖8u-v‖ & \\le ‖8u‖+‖-v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖8u-v‖ & \\le 8‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 35 & \\le 8‖u‖+11 \\\\ 24 & \\le 8‖u‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2391612a-ee27-5cb2-a194-9b51e6fec1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Pythagorean Theorem and the Cauchy-Schwarz and Triangle Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2b45db1-5e23-5430-b71a-305288456649" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309720} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9d0280-7968-5d3b-afc6-cac297e17077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309721} {:answer/id #uuid "e6020dc3-7d16-5e91-b61f-e9a7eb272f61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309722} {:answer/id #uuid "e868f26a-188e-5190-b027-255826c602b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309723} {:answer/id #uuid "cce29948-b4f6-5b02-bcf6-ab21aa28cae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e868f26a-188e-5190-b027-255826c602b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309723} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b7a29b2-35c0-5506-93cc-dab35bc0f59a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ccc53bc-857f-503f-8921-535a0b5ce1cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-140461" :question/problem "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=39$ and $‖v‖=7$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}39 & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (7)+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =7‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 7‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =7‖u‖+(‖u‖+7) \\\\  & =8‖u‖+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}39 & \\le 8‖u‖+7 \\\\ 32 & \\le 8‖u‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04b8c8285d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a52c3b15-7f3a-54cf-b50d-d344d26b8685" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{337}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131289} {:answer/id #uuid "e102a30a-58e9-56ca-b603-3fd3d685511b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131290} {:answer/id #uuid "e473836c-095d-522d-9a46-80145fe4328d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131291} {:answer/id #uuid "3e2492ad-f832-557b-a75e-8ae82d578300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131292} {:answer/id #uuid "4be2ca3b-dea8-5f2c-ab94-4eac8e635fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e102a30a-58e9-56ca-b603-3fd3d685511b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131290} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fa37048-9b16-5f4d-905e-b7cd97665ef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78f436e6-da8d-594d-9217-c77afac12ee6" :question/math-academy-id "q-39412" :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖v‖=7$ and $‖2u+v‖=25.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $2u$ is orthogonal to $v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =‖2u{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =(2‖u‖)^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (25)^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+(7)^{2} \\\\ 625 & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+49 \\\\ 576 & =4‖u{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =144\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖u‖=12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2391612a-ee27-5cb2-a194-9b51e6fec1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Pythagorean Theorem and the Cauchy-Schwarz and Triangle Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad0b60a4-08fa-552b-baa7-d6379986f121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309727} {:answer/id #uuid "d1590ba7-c219-5ad9-8fab-b1cda1d515d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309728} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6df9e1-b24b-5691-b671-ba53374460f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309729} {:answer/id #uuid "5f4d1931-6c52-538c-8023-d0ede89415aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309730} {:answer/id #uuid "290ad22d-0376-59fb-9e5b-f653f01d558c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "290ad22d-0376-59fb-9e5b-f653f01d558c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309731} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a40b6ea-2245-512f-ba22-45998bc16202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c491862-6cc2-5142-91ba-7a0b72655537" :question/math-academy-id "q-39608" :question/problem "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=34$ and $‖v‖=6$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}34 & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (6)+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =6‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 6‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =6‖u‖+(‖u‖+6) \\\\  & =7‖u‖+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}34 & \\le 7‖u‖+6 \\\\ 28 & \\le 7‖u‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2391612a-ee27-5cb2-a194-9b51e6fec1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Pythagorean Theorem and the Cauchy-Schwarz and Triangle Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5f8016f-6ef7-57c4-8ffa-937e9afa02d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131343} {:answer/id #uuid "01b1041b-b79e-57d5-95e7-f4b05974c395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131344} {:answer/id #uuid "497f1cd8-8f6f-5fd9-b0f3-a5bcd8b9ef29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131345} {:answer/id #uuid "66e27020-a003-5e9f-b39e-dd0ec7a7b70c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131346} {:answer/id #uuid "7e51aebc-db57-5617-a11b-53d382973fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e51aebc-db57-5617-a11b-53d382973fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131347} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a565d2f-881d-59ff-83e9-7acd86e5fbdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0481f3fc-bbad-5359-bc8f-155c905afe87" :question/math-academy-id "q-39610" :question/problem "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2}=50$ and $‖u‖=‖w‖=4$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖?$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}50 & =|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v⊥w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\  & =17‖v{‖}^{2}+16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}50 & \\le 17‖v‖+16 \\\\ 34 & \\le 17‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 2 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $2\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $\\sqrt{2}\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2391612a-ee27-5cb2-a194-9b51e6fec1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Pythagorean Theorem and the Cauchy-Schwarz and Triangle Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fe8a947-6153-58fe-b65f-ad4219945521" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309734} {:answer/id #uuid "acc98e97-cd60-54e8-a31f-9e57b454e8a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309735} {:answer/id #uuid "38da9464-c2aa-510f-bfc5-ce507c75360a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309736} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa53caf-fe66-5ffe-9d17-2e552d6995c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309737} {:answer/id #uuid "c321f81d-98f4-54ba-83a4-ff4ce0b89455" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38da9464-c2aa-510f-bfc5-ce507c75360a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309736} :answer-field/id #uuid "81c4c843-e8e8-5f58-ab16-fd3ed9cb0715" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47488a47-14a3-5678-954b-f24ebcdf0f1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40243" :question/problem "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=19$ and $‖v‖=9$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19 & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (9)+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =9‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 9‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =9‖u‖+(‖u‖+9) \\\\  & =10‖u‖+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19 & \\le 10‖u‖+9 \\\\ 10 & \\le 10‖u‖ \\\\ 1 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae3aec8-4d20-5467-9ced-2a9c1bda3afd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minimum Value Using the Triangle Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125af8d5-bf83-5106-a1ae-303b53449930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131643} {:answer/id #uuid "295fe950-b638-54e3-b7f4-badeb7a832f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131644} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd215e9-b290-5424-a3b8-f31f4d439c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131645} {:answer/id #uuid "483c7c4a-d2f0-5f4e-868a-c08d561e4b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131646} {:answer/id #uuid "7330b971-0d9e-5159-b9f7-94ab74ceebc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7330b971-0d9e-5159-b9f7-94ab74ceebc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131647} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa32156d-18c0-5bd2-b442-3977cc1a663e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b171c49-12bc-5a9e-82c9-5de048b43a17" :question/math-academy-id "q-40244" :question/problem "Given that $‖7u+v‖=32$ and $‖v‖=4$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖7u+v‖ & \\le ‖7u‖+‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖7u+v‖ & \\le 7‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 32 & \\le 7‖u‖+4 \\\\ 28 & \\le 7‖u‖ \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04b8c8285d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5bc08a9-b6e4-54bc-b4aa-017bd50a47f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309741} {:answer/id #uuid "72e53761-85c7-5709-8eac-8b72e55471e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309742} {:answer/id #uuid "7d1689fd-76be-5cec-ae3f-b7cd3071ad95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309743} {:answer/id #uuid "ef791f48-0f71-5920-95e1-d516d1c7c224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309744} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2e85a1-ccd1-5d42-b480-f714b3135378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef791f48-0f71-5920-95e1-d516d1c7c224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309744} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9b1900a-9bd6-5d03-b339-2a38dcac2bbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de123b7e-6906-5d9f-ab1d-3d3f8fdc4d35" :question/math-academy-id "q-40263" :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖u‖=6\\sqrt{2}$ and $‖u+2v‖=6\\sqrt{6}.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $u$ is orthogonal to $2v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+‖2v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖u‖+(‖2v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (6\\sqrt{6})^{2} & =(6\\sqrt{2})^{2}+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 216 & =72+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 144 & =4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309746 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04b8c8285d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da4cff1c-633c-5daa-b2c6-a12b1dfe29fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309748} {:answer/id #uuid "a332669e-4c33-5a9a-b676-e08755f41618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309749} {:answer/id #uuid "b15d5cb9-0771-5882-9b52-9799560c4883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309750} {:answer/id #uuid "3b5cf131-5b5c-59dc-8868-3fbb8073e006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1\\,013}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309751} {:answer/id #uuid "4c852026-e34a-5359-a25c-c27a20ddb5bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a332669e-4c33-5a9a-b676-e08755f41618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309749} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae948f1d-79d0-56c9-b205-f6111f5db881" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fd4f0c8-283c-51b8-8f02-c3a374eace40" :question/math-academy-id "q-40264" :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖u‖=15$ and $‖u+\\sqrt{5}v‖=75.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $u$ is orthogonal to $\\sqrt{5}v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+‖\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5}‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖u+\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (75)^{2} & =(15)^{2}+5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 5\\,625 & =225+5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 5\\,400 & =5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =1\\,080\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=6\\sqrt{30}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae3aec8-4d20-5467-9ced-2a9c1bda3afd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minimum Value Using the Triangle Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e10044e-ed22-54b7-a9ae-c4df3896e1e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309755} {:answer/id #uuid "5d7ceaf9-cb2c-5167-b93a-73afdfe51055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309756} {:answer/id #uuid "df7d0282-f017-5c4d-a3f0-b56d8a9acf6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309757} {:answer/id #uuid "45d87428-6a1d-58ac-9d03-35866485327e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309758} {:answer/id #uuid "4571f5ae-bc56-58ec-9ede-7eb63e137bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45d87428-6a1d-58ac-9d03-35866485327e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309758} :answer-field/id #uuid "2203298a-2380-54c5-a1a8-04645bb1b425" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e93d9252-42f5-532b-823c-8aea26cbb807" :question/math-academy-id "q-40899" :question/problem "Given that $‖4u+v‖=29$ and $‖v‖=5$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖4u+v‖ & \\le ‖4u‖+‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖4u+v‖ & \\le 4‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 29 & \\le 4‖u‖+5 \\\\ 24 & \\le 4‖u‖ \\\\ 6 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04b8c8285d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b68311f-1e34-5326-81be-6ae8a0a6ffd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309762} {:answer/id #uuid "af3ec434-f6c1-5952-87d4-5c1391009944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309763} {:answer/id #uuid "ef3a053b-a917-5545-95ee-80db3f8533ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309764} {:answer/id #uuid "51197bc6-1d5a-52a3-9460-389bdf9b20b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309765} {:answer/id #uuid "c67f85ab-13c6-526d-ba32-441b0d97cd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51197bc6-1d5a-52a3-9460-389bdf9b20b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309765} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3f5eed8-582f-569a-93c8-d30fc5305fa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c4d610b-a232-57ed-9e2f-94b7dce72e81" :question/math-academy-id "q-74106" :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖v‖=4$ and $‖3u+2v‖=17.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $3u$ is orthogonal to $2v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖3u{‖}^{2}+‖2v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3u+2v{‖}^{2} & =(3‖u‖)^{2}+(2‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖3u+2v{‖}^{2} & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (17)^{2} & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+4(4)^{2} \\\\ 289 & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+4\\cdot 16 \\\\ 289 & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+64 \\\\ 225 & =9‖u{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖u‖=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04b8c8285d89" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector Using the Pythagorean Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cabfc52-f16c-52f4-83d6-89f91b8adc04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309769} {:answer/id #uuid "51c545b0-5640-5a8f-b657-82a3bf9a1cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309770} {:answer/id #uuid "e39e7ed4-bb25-53c3-8a5a-54ce81da77fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309771} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7b3e3c-358c-59b3-a09c-2842c5975b58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309772} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d34f44-0556-5d04-9e90-e996f721860a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0d34f44-0556-5d04-9e90-e996f721860a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309773} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a177a4-bc16-578c-974a-ea68efc9c133" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9c77086-5264-54dd-9623-65feabc3a826" :question/math-academy-id "q-74109" :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖u‖=4$ and $‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v‖=\\sqrt{182}.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $\\sqrt{2}u$ is orthogonal to $\\sqrt{3}v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2} & =‖\\sqrt{2}u{‖}^{2}+‖\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{2}‖u‖)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2} & =2‖u{‖}^{2}+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (\\sqrt{182})^{2} & =2(4)^{2}+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 182 & =2\\cdot 16+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 182 & =32+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 150 & =3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=5\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae3aec8-4d20-5467-9ced-2a9c1bda3afd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minimum Value Using the Triangle Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd91940e-f509-5a42-a014-4fac899a9916" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309776} {:answer/id #uuid "bb50243f-f27a-5732-ad22-fdb761c767b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309777} {:answer/id #uuid "166b41b6-702c-5823-9970-5e6c4876a760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309778} {:answer/id #uuid "d22db3fc-4ed3-5008-9174-cb97b678adff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309779} {:answer/id #uuid "1cc2ad41-9941-5d2c-99dd-ecf427cd2971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd91940e-f509-5a42-a014-4fac899a9916" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309776} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9bc8519-5c29-5b44-a192-95af85774026" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61513b82-911a-5ff9-bb4e-85b029111b65" :question/math-academy-id "q-74177" :question/problem "Given that $‖u+5v‖=19$ and $‖u‖=4$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+5v‖ & \\le ‖u‖+‖5v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+5v‖ & \\le ‖u‖+5‖v‖ \\\\ 19 & \\le 4+5‖v‖ \\\\ 15 & \\le 5‖v‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$ is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2391612a-ee27-5cb2-a194-9b51e6fec1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Combining the Pythagorean Theorem and the Cauchy-Schwarz and Triangle Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d37c882f-e260-5a29-8c97-9a35b7408443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309783} {:answer/id #uuid "d05d7d9c-3ce0-5045-8952-1c3c67011f39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309784} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6dfc9f-ef8f-54bb-8608-2c5733692844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309785} {:answer/id #uuid "04d8a5c1-d829-542e-9206-9951103bfa62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309786} {:answer/id #uuid "6e07238e-ae6f-51bf-8644-94ef27697c95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d37c882f-e260-5a29-8c97-9a35b7408443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309783} :answer-field/id #uuid "82fbf3b5-a6c7-5638-a0ea-2990e64c070d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bd88faa5-6854-51de-a79d-d62db631781d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74191" :question/problem "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2}=62$ and $‖u‖=‖w‖=3$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖?$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}62 & ={|u\\cdot v|}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v⊥w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9‖v{‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+4(‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2}) \\\\  & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+4(‖v{‖}^{2}+{3}^{2}) \\\\  & =13‖v{‖}^{2}+36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}62 & \\le 13‖v{‖}^{2}+36 \\\\ 26 & \\le 13‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 2 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $2\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $\\sqrt{2}\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$"}]}
